    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d504">

                <pb facs="0455" n="339" xml:id="pg339"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/853.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Livingston to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Cape Haitien</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 21, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Army of Theodore evacuated town last night leaving no police or other organized
                    forces. Marines and sailors from <hi rendition="#italic">Wheeling</hi> patrolled
                    streets throughout night; sailors reembarked this morning; marines remain at
                    Consulate. One division Government army entered this morning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Livingston</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
